 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S444-009\", \"clauses\": {\"create\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"Create a pattern that starts at {first_term} and uses the rule: {rule}. Which sequence shows this pattern?\", \"reasoning\": \"F02 opens with the task verb Create. Its rule slot is nested F08, so a create task with a stated Add or Subtract rule is produced. F02 has no pattern_label slot, so it cannot pair a label with a contradictory rule.\"}, \"increasing_decreasing\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"Create a pattern that starts at {first_term} and uses the rule: {rule}. Which sequence shows this pattern?\", \"reasoning\": \"The F08 v domain (Add or Subtract, basis the rule's direction) sets the rule's direction. Add gives an increasing sequence and Subtract gives a decreasing one, so F02 produces both properties with no contradiction.\"}, \"patterns\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F02\", \"template\": \"Create a pattern that starts at {first_term} and uses the rule: {rule}. Which sequence shows this pattern?\", \"reasoning\": \"F02 names the object as a pattern in its template, and the question asks the learner to identify the sequence that shows this pattern.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F03\", \"F06\", \"F07\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"Start at {first_term} and create {v} {pattern_label} with the rule: {rule}. Which pattern did you create?\", \"Which sequence correctly shows {v} {pattern_label} starting at {first_term} and following the rule: {rule}?\", \"You want to create {v} {pattern_label} where the rule is: {rule}. Which sequence correctly creates it?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F03, F06 and F07 fill pattern_label from its own fixed domain of the three labels (decreasing pattern, increasing pattern, repeating pattern) and fill rule from nested F08, which prints only Add or Subtract with a step from 1 to 5. These are separate domains with no derivation linking them, so every label can pair with every rule direction. A repeating pattern can therefore be stated with an Add or Subtract rule, and an increasing or decreasing label can be stated with the opposite direction. Each is a self-contradictory statement for a learner. The article slot v (a or an) is also a separate domain from pattern_label with no derivation, so mismatched combinations such as an article that does not fit the label can print. F02 has no label slot and pairs only Add or Subtract with a start value, so it is consistent and passes. The hint families F01, F04 and F05 and the answer and option families F09 and F10 show no fault in the packet. Observed answers from the printed runs are all non-negative, so I did not flag negative values.\"}",
